# ---------- AWM, REF-00468, US
A=dict(ref='REF-00468',jur='US',lens='MOB',ls='section',
       lensnote=LN%('MOB','the report measures wheelchair and scooter users, the population these widths serve'))
def awm(p,val,unit,cmp_,role,quote,sec,loc,setting,note,pdfp):
    r(**A,p=p,val=val,unit=unit,cmp=cmp_,role=role,quote=quote,sec='Anthropometry of Wheeled Mobility Project Final Report, '+sec,setting=setting,loc=loc,locnote=pdfp,note=note+A['lensnote'])
awm(5,'2500','mm','>=','finding','The 360-degree turning diameter would have to be increased to 2500 mm (a little over 98 in.) to accommodate our entire study sample.','section 3.3.13',('3.3.13',None,None),'360-degree turn in a confined space; whole sample of 495 users','Quantity: diameter that would accommodate every user in the study sample for a 360-degree turn; the report states it against the US standard of 1525 mm, which fewer than half of its manual and powered wheelchair users completed within. A finding about the sample, not a recommended standard.','PDF page 65 of 173; report page 61')
awm(5,'1900','mm',None,'finding','In fact, the tightest 360 turn performed by a scooter user was 1900 mm (75 in.) in diameter!','section 3.3.13',('3.3.13',None,None),'360-degree turn; scooter users','Quantity: smallest diameter in which any scooter user in the sample completed a 360-degree turn. A measured minimum for one device class, not a requirement.','PDF page 65 of 173; report page 61')
awm(4,'1000','mm','>=','claim','We recommend revising the ADA-ABA standard for 90-degree turning width to 1000 mm (39 in.) which would accommodate at least 95% of our sample.','section 4.3.5.1',('4.3.5.1',None,None),'width of a passage at a 90-degree (L) turn','Quantity: passage width at a 90-degree turn; the authors\' recommendation for a standard. Their Figure 4-4 text puts the current ADA requirement at 915 mm and 50 percent of manual and powered chair users needing 850 mm. Whether a width at a turn is parameter 4 or a term of its own is deferred (observation 98).','PDF page 97 of 173; report page 93')
awm(4,'1700','mm','>=','finding','Our findings indicated that a width of 1700 mm (67 in.) would accommodate 95% of manual and power wheelchair users and 90% of the scooter users.','section 4.3.5.2',('4.3.5.2',None,None),'width of a space bounded by two parallel walls or three walls, 180-degree turn','Quantity: width accommodating 95 percent of manual and powered wheelchair users and 90 percent of scooter users in a 180-degree turn. A finding; the authors note the ADA-ABA has no clearance for this turn and the 1525 mm turning space is used instead. Deferred term as for observation 98.','PDF page 99 of 173; report page 95')
awm(4,'1095','mm','>=','claim','We recommend using this approach in future ADA-ABA standards with a minimum width of 1095 mm (43 in.) which would accommodate more than 95% of all WhMD users in the sample.','section 4.3.5.3',('4.3.5.3',None,None),'uniform width for a 180-degree turn around an obstacle','Quantity: minimum uniform width (entry aisle, turning area depth and egress aisle equal) for a 180-degree turn around an obstacle; the authors\' recommendation. Deferred term as for observation 98.','PDF page 100 of 173; report page 96')
# ---------- ES TMA/851/2021, REF-01028
E=dict(ref='REF-01028',jur='ES',lens='ALL',ls='section',locnote_base='BOE-A-2021-13488 consolidated text as retrieved in batch 23')
def es(p,val,unit,cmp_,role,claim_type,quote,sec,loc,setting,note,why):
    r(ref='REF-01028',jur='ES',lens='ALL',ls='section',p=p,val=val,unit=unit,cmp=cmp_,role=role,ctype=claim_type,quote=quote,sec='Orden TMA/851/2021, '+sec,setting=setting,loc=loc,locnote='BOE consolidated text, article '+loc[0],note=note+LN%('ALL',why),lang='es')
W='the clause names no population'
es(4,'1.80','m','>=','claim','numerical','En todo su desarrollo poseerá una anchura libre de paso no inferior a 1,80 m, que garantice el giro, cruce y cambio de dirección de las personas, independientemente de sus características o modo de desplazamiento.','article 5.2.b',('5','2','b'),'accessible pedestrian route in urbanised public space','Quantity: minimum clear width of an accessible pedestrian route (itinerario peatonal accesible), outdoors in public space, not a building corridor. The clause gives the reason: turning, passing and changing direction. Unit as stated (metres, comma decimal in the source).',"the clause says 'independientemente de sus características o modo de desplazamiento'")
es(11,'2.20','m','>=','claim','numerical','En todo su desarrollo poseerá una altura libre de paso no inferior a 2,20 m.','article 5.2.c',('5','2','c'),'accessible pedestrian route in urbanised public space','Quantity: minimum clear height of an accessible pedestrian route. The same 2,20 m recurs for rest areas (art 6), parks (art 7) and ramps (art 14.7); not filed again (rule 5).',W)
es(5,'1.50','m','>=','claim','numerical','Contarán con un espacio libre de obstáculos donde pueda inscribirse un círculo de 1,50 m de diámetro, como mínimo, delante de la puerta de acceso y dicho espacio no podrá coincidir, ni con el itinerario peatonal accesible, ni con el área barrida por la apertura de la puerta de la cabina.','article 34.2.a',('34','2','a'),'in front of the door of an accessible public toilet cabin, outside','Quantity: minimum diameter of the circle to be inscribed in the obstacle-free space before the cabin door; it may not coincide with the accessible route or the door swing. A circle of this diameter, not stated as a wheelchair turning space in this clause.',W)
es(5,'1.50','m','>=','claim','numerical','Junto a la puerta habrá un espacio libre de obstáculos que permita inscribir en toda su altura un círculo de 1,50 m de diámetro mínimo, siendo la altura mínima en el interior de la cabina de 2,20 m.','article 34.3.a',('34','3','a'),'inside an accessible public toilet cabin, beside the door','Quantity: minimum diameter of the obstacle-free circle inside the cabin, over its full height. The same sentence states the cabin interior height (see the parameter 11 row).',W)
es(11,'2.20','m','>=','claim','numerical','siendo la altura mínima en el interior de la cabina de 2,20 m.','article 34.3.a',('34','3','a'),'inside an accessible public toilet cabin','Quantity: minimum interior height of the cabin. Read from the same sentence as the parameter 5 row inside the cabin.',W)
es(9,'80','cm','>=','claim','numerical','La puerta de acceso será abatible hacia el exterior o corredera, tendrá una anchura libre de paso mínima de 80 cm y su mecanismo de cierre será de fácil manejo, posibilitando su apertura desde fuera en caso de emergencia.','article 34.2.b',('34','2','b'),'access door of an accessible public toilet cabin','Quantity: minimum clear passage width of the cabin door. Unit as stated (centimetres).',W)
es(6,'25','N','<=','claim','numerical','En todo caso el mecanismo de apertura no requerirá una fuerza superior a 25 N y el sistema de cierre será retardado.','article 28.b',('28',None,'b'),'opening mechanism of a street litter bin or container','Quantity: maximum force to operate the opening mechanism of a litter bin or waste container on the pedestrian route. Not a door; the only force figure in the order.',W)
es(6,None,None,None,'finding','absent','Los mecanismos de accionamiento de lavabos, duchas y mecanismos de descarga de inodoros serán pulsadores de gran superficie accionables con el puño o con el codo, o palancas de fácil manejo y requerirán poco esfuerzo.','article 34.3.f',('34','3','f'),'controls in an accessible public toilet cabin','Absence: the clause that governs the operating controls of the cabin states poor force qualitatively (poco esfuerzo, little effort) and gives no figure, in an order that gives 25 N for litter bin openings. Found by keyword search (fuerza, esfuerzo, N, newton) over the whole text; the text was not read end to end.',W)
es(8,None,None,None,'finding','absent','Todos los montantes verticales u horizontales que delimiten el itinerario estarán recubiertos por materiales protectores frente a golpes y su visibilidad estará garantizada mediante colores de alto contraste.','article 39.2',('39','2',None),'temporary works scaffold uprights on a pedestrian route','Absence: contrast is required in words (colores de alto contraste, high-contrast colours) and no light reflectance value or luminance difference is stated. Keyword search over the whole text (contraste, luminancia, reflectancia, LRV) found no figure; the text was not read end to end.',W)
# ---------- KR 별표1, REF-01031
